      <a href="#allergen-free">Other Top Allergens</a>
      <a href="#how-we-picked">How We Picked</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          The best soy-free protein powder for most people is Transparent Labs Grass-Fed Whey Isolate, which uses sunflower lecithin instead of soy lecithin and gives 28 g of protein per scoop, per the brand. If you avoid dairy too, Vega Sport Premium Protein gives about 30 g of soy-free plant protein. The thing to watch is not soy protein but soy lecithin, the emulsifier in many popular wheys, including Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard per its label.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="quick-comparison" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
