          <p>
            The short version: soy turns up in protein powder in two places, as soy protein isolate in plant blends and as soy lecithin, the emulsifier that helps whey mix. Transparent Labs Grass-Fed Whey Isolate is our top soy-free pick because it uses sunflower lecithin instead, per label listings at the time of writing. Naked Whey has no lecithin at all, Klean Isolate is the NSF-certified option, and Vega Sport and OWYN cover buyers who need soy-free and dairy-free together. The table lines up the seven picks.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Product</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Protein per serving</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Emulsifier / soy status</th>
